{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":203510,"ns":0,"title":"Social constructionism","extract":"Social constructionism is a term used in sociology, social ontology, and communication theory. The term can serve somewhat different functions in each field; however, the foundation of this theoretical framework suggests various facets of social reality—such as concepts, beliefs, norms and values—are formed through continuous interactions and negotiations among society's members, rather than empirical observation of physical reality.","description":"Sociological theory regarding shared understandings","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}